  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Participatory Roadmap towards a more conducive environment for organic compost in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment supports the development of a participatory roadmap to foster an enabling environment for the production, use, marketing, and wider adoption of organic compost in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire.The approach is based on structured multi-stakeholder engagement, involving farmers, traditional authorities, youth groups, private sector representatives, government institutions, policymakers, non-governmental organisations (NGOs), and international partners. Through focus group discussions and multistakeholder workshops, the project maps the compost ecosystem, assesses stakeholder perspectives and constraints, and reviews relevant legislation and existing initiatives.The resulting roadmap provides coordinated and evidence-based recommendations to promote favourable policy conditions and a level playing field for stakeholders across the organic compost value chain.</narrative>
  </description>
